Add wasm_runtime_set_thread_native_stack_boundary().

By default every exec env records the native stack boundary of the OS thread stack
(`os_thread_get_stack_boundary()`). For embedders whose "threads" run on their own
stacks (e.g. Julia tasks, which have their own stacks), this boundary is wrong, and it
cannot be fixed via `wasm_runtime_set_native_stack_boundary()` for exec envs that the
runtime creates internally (e.g. to run start functions during instantiation). This adds
a per-thread override that is used for all exec envs subsequently created on the calling
thread (NULL restores the default).

Upstream: not yet reported.

